# GEOZITY - ACCOUNT AND LOCAL CONFIGURATION GUIDE
#
# WHAT TO DO
# 1. Open the existing .env.local beside this file (in the project root).
# 2. Add the missing names below and paste their values after =.
# 3. Keep your existing Geoapify and Render values. Do not overwrite .env.local.
# 4. Leave AI, voice switches, and limits at the defaults for now.
# 5. Save the file and tell me "Keys saved". I will check the connections next.
#
# This example contains no credentials. Actual values belong only in .env.local.
# Never paste keys into chat or add VITE_ to any secret variable name.
# .env.local and globe/.dev.vars are excluded from Git.

# REQUIRED FOR THE NEW GLOBE APP: LIVE PLACE SEARCH
# https://myprojects.geoapify.com/
# Sign in > choose your Geozity project > API Keys > copy its API key.
# Already configured locally: keep your existing value in .env.local.
GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=

# REQUIRED FOR THE NEW GLOBE APP: SUPABASE
# https://supabase.com/dashboard
# Use a dedicated Geozity project on the Free plan, not another app's database.
# Choose a nearby available region. Keep the database password privately;
# the running app does NOT need that password or a database connection string.
#
# Project URL: open the project's Connect dialog and copy the Project URL.
# It looks like https://<project-reference>.supabase.co (not the dashboard URL).
SUPABASE_URL=
# Server key: project > Settings > API Keys > Secret keys > create/copy a key.
# Name it Geozity server if asked. The preferred key starts with sb_secret_.
# Do not use the publishable key, anon key, or personal access token here.
# This is a private master key; the server uses it, never the website browser.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional compatibility: if you already have a legacy service_role key,
# it can go below instead of SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY. You only need ONE server key.
# Leave this blank when using the preferred secret key above.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Setup only: https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
# Never upload this management token to the website or application server.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Saving keys does not create database tables or change existing records.
# I will check the target project before setting up Geozity's usage counter.

# OPTIONAL: ELEVENLABS VOICE INPUT AND SPOKEN REPLIES
# https://elevenlabs.io/app
# API key: sign in > Developers > API Keys > create a key named Geozity.
# Allow Speech to Text and Text to Speech if the key editor offers permissions.
# Set a small usage/credit limit on this key if your account offers it.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Voice ID: Voices > My Voices > choose a voice > three dots > Copy voice ID.
# Choose a default voice available to your plan. This is an ID, not a voice name.
# Needed for spoken replies; transcription uses the API key without a voice ID.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
# Keep these model settings; no model signup or separate key is required.
ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=scribe_v3
ELEVENLABS_TTS_MODEL=eleven_v4
# If voice ID is blank, the app uses the documented premade George voice.
# The onboarding CLI can keep ELEVENLABS_API_KEY in globe/.env.local;
# setup:local reads that file as well. No need to copy the key by hand.

# OPTIONAL: SARVAM FOR INDIAN AND MIXED-LANGUAGE VOICE
# https://dashboard.sarvam.ai/
# Sign in > API Keys > create/copy your API subscription key.
# This is the Model APIs key, not a Voice Agents phone/calling account token.
SARVAM_API_KEY=
# Explicit latest recorded-audio and speech-generation models (checked 15 Nov 2026).
SARVAM_STT_MODEL=saaras:v4
SARVAM_TTS_MODEL=bulbul:v4-flash
# The app returns an editable English translation of Indian/mixed speech.
# Answers are currently English; speech generation does not translate text.
SARVAM_TTS_LANGUAGE=en-IN
# Leave disabled until account access, privacy, license, and quotas are checked.
# Free usage is limited; the listed commercial license is on a paid plan.
# Geozity does not save recordings. Each selected voice provider has its own retention policy.
ENABLE_VOICE=false
DAILY_VOICE_SECONDS_LIMIT=0
DAILY_SPEECH_CHAR_LIMIT=0

# OPTIONAL INTENT AI: DIRECT SARVAM, USING SARVAM_API_KEY ABOVE
# Understands phrasing; actual places always come from the map provider.
# No DeepSpace account or separate OpenAI key is required.
# Fast Sarvam model for interactive requests, verified 15 November 2026.
ENABLE_AI=false
AI_MODEL=sarvam-105b-conversations
DAILY_AI_CALL_LIMIT=0

# SAFE DEFAULTS: THESE ARE SETTINGS, NOT VALUES TO GET FROM AN ACCOUNT
# Shared daily map-call allowance, not number of searches; a search can use 2 calls.
DAILY_MAP_CALL_LIMIT=200
# Set true to pause external search and voice provider calls.
DISABLE_EXTERNAL_PROVIDERS=false
MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty
# Generated locally by globe's setup script; no online account needed.
# Leave blank unless a technician is deliberately supplying a private random value.
SESSION_HMAC_SECRET=

# AFTER SAVING (I can run these steps for you):
# Open a terminal in the globe folder and run pnpm dev (it runs setup automatically).
# setup:local copies only approved app settings into ignored globe/.dev.vars.
# It generates SESSION_HMAC_SECRET, keeps Render credentials out, and never prints keys.
# Database initialization is also required before search works on the new app.
# This local file does not update hosted Cloudflare, Render, or Vercel settings.
# The existing public Vercel/Render app is unchanged.
# Local voice controls need ENABLE_VOICE=true plus nonzero daily voice/speech limits.
# Keep them off until the usage-counter database setup and provider privacy/license
# settings have been checked; the separate test:voice:live command uses short samples.

# EXISTING FLASK APP ONLY - KEPT FOR COMPATIBILITY

# Local server port; the single-server startup command follows this setting.
PORT=5000

# Legacy examples retained for compatibility; the current app does not read these.
# Parsing is deterministic. An AI key does not enable an external AI service.
FLASK_ENV=development
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional upstream replacements. Defaults are the existing public providers.
# Review provider usage rules and contact identification before public hosting.
NOMINATIM_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search
OVERPASS_URLS=https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter,https://overpass.kumi.systems/api/interpreter,https://lz4.overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
PHOTON_URL=https://photon.komoot.io
